WEBVTT

NOTE Text follows the V006 documented narration and dialogue windows. Some on-site speech outside documented windows is not transcribed.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:09.600
InstAgent is an agent operating system for heterogeneous multi-robot collaboration. It organizes different robot capabilities into executable collaboration programs.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.700
Our contributions span a physical agent OS, collaborative self-improvement, and real-robot evaluation.

3
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.700
Collab-RSI improves collaboration programs through execution feedback and retains verified revisions.

4
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:31.600
Guidance, navigation, and loading are organized as behavior trees with defined steps and dependencies. Programs and their usage conditions form reusable experience.

5
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.700
A guidance program specifies its destination input and the conditions for use.

6
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.100
For a new guidance and delivery task,

7
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.600
the system composes existing experience.

8
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.650
Hello.

9
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:49.383
What can I do for you?

10
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:51.683
Find a seat for me with G1.

11
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:54.783
Please follow me.

12
00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:03.567
Here is your seat. Please have a seat.

13
00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.749
Bring me some Coke and chips.

14
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:13.517
Sure. I'll arrange for Coke and chips to be delivered to your destination.

15
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.700
Go2 heads to the shelf.

16
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:25.850
The bimanual robot, Split ALOHA, handles loading, placing chips into the basket carried by Go2.

17
00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:33.833
It then adds a Coke, completing the load for Go2 to transport.

18
00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:43.933
Go2 carries both items back to the seating area.

19
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:52.333
The user receives both items, completing the task.

20
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:01.700
Shared Memory gives collaboration a common view of the environment. An exploration request brings observations from different robots together.

21
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:13.700
The map marks robot locations and their spatial relationships. Shared Memory organizes spatial information into a common environmental context that supports collaboration.

22
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.600
Users can speak directly with G1.

23
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:39.000
Requests can also come from a phone. After receiving the instruction, Go2 moves toward the shelf while the interface displays task status.

24
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:46.400
The mobile interface keeps users informed as the robot carries out their request.

25
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:54.400
On the web, a user asks ALOHA to move its lift to one hundred millimeters.

26
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:59.400
Camera views and point clouds show the action as it unfolds.

